I get the impression that Odin would get very upset with you
if you tried to invoke his name in a temple to Loki.

As far as an intrinsic second sight for the bless/cursedness of
items, I think I'd prefer to keep it as a priest thing -- helps
to keep the classes distinct.  Higher-level characters of other
classes do acquire other ways of determining the status.

I've noticed that by the time I get strong enough to kill a priest,
cursedness plays no role in my interest in an item.  If it's cursed,
I'll probably uncurse it (unless for some arcane reason I'd like
to keep it cursed).  Uncursed items I tend to bless before use
(by that point in the game anyway).  So, I have no problems without
knowing a-priori whether an item is cursed or not -- I'll take it anyway.

However, I must say that I was rather intrigued by your suggestion
to add it to the other "blessing".  Maybe that would make it less
of a bane.  For now, however, it makes a nice priest class distinction.
Otherwise, we might start seeing 'Jane's book of Gems' and
'Jane's Book of Medieval Weapons' (since other classes can
readily identify these categories).

